Hello Mikhail,

Yes it is possible, please see the help file of:
?makeChart

Whether constructing the matrix your way or the makeChart() way, the function solveChart() gives you the solution(s):

> solveChart(mat)
     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    1
[2,]    2    2
[3,]    3    6
[4,]    4    7
[5,]    5    8

Besides the solution you mention {A, B, C, D, E}, your matrix is also covered by {A, B, F, G, H}.

I hope this helps,
Adrian

